invariant: INV-17
file: p256_scalar.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_scalar
reason: p256_scalar_reduced_mask returns without wiping its difference,
  which is its operand less n modulo 2^256. The signer calls it on the
  private key and on each candidate nonce, and the key exchange on its
  private scalar, so the array gives each of them to whoever reads it.
  Its lifetime ends with the call, so no vector reads it.
  proof/p256_scalar_harness.c counts the bytes ct_wipe is handed and
  requires one array's worth after the call. Each run is a proof, so this
  belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
    ct_wipe(discard, sizeof discard);
    return mask;
--- new
    return mask;
